Disable the webview service worker, and relax its CSP to match.

A webview runs in a cross-origin iframe. Android's WebView will let a
ServiceWorkerClient intercept the worker script, but activation never completes
there: controllerchange does not fire, workerReady never resolves, and the
webview stays blank indefinitely. Resources are served through
shouldInterceptRequest on the Kotlin side instead, so the worker has nothing to
do here even when it does start.

The CSP change is a consequence, not a preference. script-src pins the inline
script by sha256, and patching that script changes its digest. Planning recorded
it as unverified whether the build recomputes the hash; it does not: nothing
under build/ touches it, and the value is byte-identical between the source file
and the packaged output. Left alone, the patched script would be blocked and
every webview would be blank for a different reason than before.

'unsafe-inline' is narrower here than it sounds: default-src stays 'none',
frame-src stays 'self', and the only inline script in the document is the one
shipped with it.

The explanatory comment sits outside the <meta> element. An earlier revision put
it between the tag name and its attributes, which breaks the element: the browser
stops parsing it as a tag and renders content="default-src 'none'; ..." as
visible text at the top of every webview, with no CSP applied at all. It was
caught on screen: the webviews rendered, but only because the policy had
silently gone missing.

diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/webview/browser/pre/index.html b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/webview/browser/pre/index.html
index 42c7c01..b54597e 100644
--- a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/webview/browser/pre/index.html
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/webview/browser/pre/index.html
@@ -4,8 +4,12 @@
 <head>
 	<meta charset="UTF-8">
 
+	<!-- script-src is 'unsafe-inline' rather than a hash because the inline script
+	     below is patched, which changes its digest. Nothing in the build recomputes
+	     this value, verified by comparing source against packaged output, so leaving
+	     the hash would block the script and blank every webview. -->
 	<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"
-		content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'sha256-FFQoOVVa2tOE3uqUvirwaMNT20TZmrHcL2aaOjJ8BUo=' 'self'; frame-src 'self'; style-src 'unsafe-inline';">
+		content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline' 'self'; frame-src 'self'; style-src 'unsafe-inline';">
 
 	<!-- Disable pinch zooming -->
 	<meta name="viewport"
@@ -33,7 +37,12 @@
